      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town sits atop a 200‑foot ridge between Goose Creek and Walnut Creek, giving it a distinctive hilltop setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Creek%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 1990s, business leaders turned Walnut Creek into an American‑Victorian themed town, a contrast to the surrounding Amish plainness.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Creek%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Walnut Creek lies at the crossroads of State Routes 39 and 515, with Route 39 leading east to New Philadelphia and west to Millersburg.",
